{"claims":[{"claim_text":"DSA recognizes that, except for the Warren Court years of 1954-1970, the Supreme Court of the United States has largely served as a conservative institution of nine, usually white men that traditionally upholds property rights over human rights.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA believes that the best way to limit the reach of the Supreme Court is to build strong and democratic social movements that both press the President and Congress to appoint progressive justices and push the judiciary to keep up with the democratic sentiments of the nation.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The militancy of the CIO in the late 1930s pushed the Court to abandon its practice of striking down government legislation regulating the power of corporations.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The militancy of the 1950s and ‘60s civil rights, feminist and anti-war movements created the preconditions for the liberal rulings of the Warren Court.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA’s primary strategy is to bring a socialist presence and analysis into the democratic movements fighting corporate power and racism, sexism and homophobia.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Democratic Supreme Court appointees vote in a somewhat more progressive manner on issues regarding race, class and gender than do Republican appointees.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"In Michigan and Wisconsin, Republican rule in every branch of state government has brought about right-to-work legislation and the denial of collective bargaining rights to public employees.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"DSA takes seriously the need in the 2014 elections to defeat reactionary Republicans at all levels of government.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
